WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
Ghosts and Goblins, the beautiful princess is kidnapped.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:10.120
Her lover, the knight, in shining armor, armed with five different weapons to fight the enemy, sets out to rescue the beautiful princess.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:32.400
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.380
I'm Mike.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.780
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:35.940
What's up, guys?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.940
Hey, hey. We're only talking about one of the hardest games of all time, dare I say?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.740
It definitely has that reputation.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.200
I think it's still up there in terms at least of reputation, of course.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:55.240
Yeah, I mean, this is pretty much the first game that I'm thinking of that's like NES hard, you know, or Nintendo hard, rather.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:04.060
Like, you know, we've had games that are just bad, badly designed, you know, but this is like an actual, like, frustratingly hard game.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:12.760
And so many, you know, YouTubers have made their careers off of starting off being like, you know, today I'm gonna play Ghosts and Goblins and freak out about it.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:24.160
And it's like, yeah, but it's very relatable because anybody who's played Ghosts and Goblins probably, you know, I want to go back for a second and talk about the 1985 end of year review that we did.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.920
Yeah. It was a special best of 1985.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.040
And I talked about Ghosts and Goblins being one of the games I'm looking forward to.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.520
I put this as one of the games that I was dreading.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.920
And I put it as looking forward to.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:35.900
We had a whole mix of.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.740
Right. And I don't know if I'm if I'm regretting that.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.260
I'll tell you one thing, though.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:45.260
I did say in that game in that in that episode that I was going to try my hardest to beat it.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:49.080
And I really think I did try my hardest, but I didn't even come close.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.960
Didn't even come close, folks.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.120
I'm not going to be pretending anything today.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:01.220
I know that there's probably like, you know, maybe one or two lucky listeners listening in right now who has beaten it.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.980
Congratulations. You're awesome.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:08.240
And hopefully you did it the right way, especially including beating it twice.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.620
But we'll get into that later.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.340
Guys, want to do some first impressions on Ghosts and Goblins?

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.820
Yeah, I guess I'll start.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.400
I like the art style.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.240
Like, I usually like the art style of these games.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:34.440
I think it's got a cool sense of humor in the way that it expresses the two hits that you get that you lose your armor and you're just in boxers.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.440
Which he also he starts the game naked.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.840
And I have. Well, I just have a couple.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.560
Yeah, it's a good time.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.720
I have a couple of complaints here.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.960
OK, because, yeah, I get he was having a good time with the princess.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.500
Right. But why the graveyard at night?

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.340
Right. Some. I don't know.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:59.540
Like, maybe she's a goth girl, you know, like it's just a cool like, hey, we're going to go to the graveyard with a picnic at midnight or three o'clock.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.780
The witching hour. Right.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.840
It's like exactly at the wrong time.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.720
You know, and by the way, I should just tell you right now that Satan's been chasing me for like the last couple of nights.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.040
If you live in a world where these monsters exist, maybe they didn't know.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.700
But if you live in a world where these monsters exist, I'm not hanging out in the graveyard.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.740
I kind of prefer to think that the monsters never existed before this moment.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.460
And like all of a sudden it's like reckoning.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.520
Like, think about it. This guy, he was naked a second ago.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.720
Now he has to like grab his arm.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.300
This is the opening cut scene, by the way.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.500
He's like naked.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.960
She gets kidnapped by Satan.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.240
And he's like, oh, shoot.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.500
Grabs his night armor.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.060
And then he's like, all right, I'm just going to go get her.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.180
Shouldn't take that long.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:43.400
And then it's like a perilous six stage journey where everything like everything that can goes wrong does go wrong.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.400
He walks into literally like one of the hardest games of all time.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.740
It's just like it's really unfortunate for this guy.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.840
Does anybody know his name?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.280
No. Arthur.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.760
OK. I wonder if he becomes King Arthur.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.860
Maybe. Maybe this is like a, you know, romancing story of the.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.800
But yeah, probably not.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:01.880
I see where you're going. Yeah.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.020
Probably not. Sean, please continue with first impressions.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:24.820
OK, so I said the couple of things that I found charming about this game, but I was right to put this on my dread list, because even though I guess over time and through the changes in how we make difficult games like in this industry.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.400
I like like new games that are hard.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.640
Like I do like Dark Souls and I do like Bloodborne and that kind of stuff.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:37.100
But I could not for the life of me get past like the second stage of this game.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.700
And I don't know if it's just because I lack determination.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.720
I need to get good or something along those lines.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.420
But I mean, I.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:49.380
I was in pain.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.380
I feel you.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:58.020
I don't think it is a matter of like determination because you can you can enter this like determined to beat this game.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.900
And then it's like, how many times are you going to see that overworld screen?

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.540
Yeah. And then your little head still on stage one.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:12.920
Right. How many times are you going to see that and be like, OK, OK, OK, this time I think I've got it.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.860
And then like, you know, Red Devil shows up and he's flying all over the screen.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.140
And you're like, I don't even think I could jump over it.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.500
Even if I like, you know, I wanted to do right now.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.180
It's like, when is my opportunity to strike Joe first impressions right off the bat?

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.140
My first impression was this is this is insanely difficult.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:40.680
And I and I was looking forward to this game because I wanted to see that punishing experience just just to just to like I didn't think I would enjoy such a punishing experience.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.460
I just thought it would be interesting to see it.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.280
But it's not punishing in the way I thought it was going to be.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.920
I thought it was going to be like you have to restart the game when you lose.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:07.080
So that's one thing I thought very early on was like, oh, it's insanely difficult, but I essentially have unlimited retries.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.840
I which made it much more bearable to me.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.660
I was very surprised to see even at a game over it.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.420
You can start at the beginning of the stage or the checkpoint.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.060
There's even a checkpoint in the stage.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:24.200
I thought the checkpoint thing was even a step further of like, like, huh, wow.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.820
They even like have that like, you know, it's obviously not saving your game.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.040
But like, as long as you have the game running, it's doing the stuff.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.200
I was like, that's pretty neat.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.280
Like even Super Mario Brothers doesn't have that.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.860
You know, you get to the end of your lives and you go all the way back to 1-1.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:45.820
I felt like I wasn't expecting to see that kind of mercy from the developers of this game, especially with the just with the reputation that it has.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.340
But I was thankful to see it.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.500
It didn't help me out that much.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:56.700
That's what I was about to say. If you don't mind me interjecting, Joe, it does help you in the sense that like you haven't you have a better chance at learning the new thing.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:11.580
But if you're just like completely stuck at a moment in the game, I don't think there's much that you can learn without like, you know, in our day and our age, you know, we're able to like go to YouTube and watch some videos about how people tackle these situations.

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:13.860
But, you know, that wasn't available to you at the time.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:20.640
And I just think like if you're going up against like, you know, let's just say those goblins, you know, from like state.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.940
I think they're in stage one, even, you know, the guys who like look like they're taking a shit.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.700
Stage two, they start.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.620
Stage two. Okay.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.440
It's like, yeah, yeah, that's true.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.980
Yeah, yeah. They're in like the building.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.780
Yeah, yeah. They're called. You have to hit them ten times.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.780
I'm glad you brought that up, Sean. They're called big men.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.840
This just keeps happening to us.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:44.340
The same guy from Kung Fu has now been mutated and tortured and cloned into the goblins you see in this game.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:50.040
But what I was getting at is, I mean, like if you're stuck on them and it's 1986, you're just done with this game.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:51.820
It doesn't matter where you are in the checkpoints.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:56.560
It's like this game only serves like a frustrating reminder is like, yeah, you've only been this far.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.520
Like it would suck if it started you way back at the beginning.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.760
Like you probably wouldn't even have a will to play the game.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.320
Exactly. I don't think anybody would have.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.480
And in fact, I'd like to know somebody who beat this game without any continues.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.280
Oh, that would be insane.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.400
Yeah. I'm sure it's happened.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.140
I'm sure it's happened for like really good Ghost and Goblins players.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.980
I'm talking more like our fan base.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.980
But Sean is watching right now.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.320
The magician has turned us into a frog.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.280
So you can't even attack.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:21.440
I don't remember that part.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:26.500
Let me ask you, though, Sean, how long did it take you to beat the first level?

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.440
The first level of the first stage?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:29.820
The first stage.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:33.340
I'm sorry. Like the first checkpoint.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.340
No, just the first full stage.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.380
OK, that took me two hours.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.960
OK, that took you two hours.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.640
And then you got to level two.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:42.960
How much of level two did you play?

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.500
Like you play for a while on level two?

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.200
I played for a while, but I didn't get to another place.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:52.480
Imagine that the first time you played level two, you died and you had to go back and do level one again.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.300
Oh, yeah. No, I would never play that game again.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:09:00.420
So I think it like I think even if you don't realize it, like the fact that you don't have to go back, like helps you a lot.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.420
Only helps you continue playing the game.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.520
Sure. That you maybe shouldn't even be playing.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:05.840
It's like Jumanji at this point.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.600
You know, it's like now I'm invested.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.120
Like I'm on the pieces.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.400
Like whatever happens in the game happens to me.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:17.020
I think it's very important that they don't send you back because it would just be demoralizing.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.400
And I mean, even more demoralizing than it already is.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:27.920
But I think it would be it would be suicide, like in terms of being a game developer to make to let that happen.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:29.460
Right. But I don't know.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:37.180
But I feel like in my in my not so educated knowledge of NES games, I thought that that happens a lot.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.100
And I could be wrong. Oh, no, it does happen a lot.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.980
I'm saying this is it's great that they offer it.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.600
Don't get me wrong. It's great that they offer it.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.740
And I'm like a console experience.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.660
It should have been the norm because the whole idea was is like I own this game.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.280
Like I'm in control of it.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:10:03.460
But, you know, at the end of the day, I agree with Sean here more than you, Joe, just because like you're the harder the game gets throughout the stages, the less likely you are to be able to push forward, regardless of how many times you tackle that situation.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.420
But, Joe, please continue with first impressions.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:13.920
I mean, really, that was that was the biggest thing was that I felt a slight bit of relief where like I can I can give this more of a shot if I just give it more time.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:20.120
Whereas I thought I was just going to hover around level one and keep dying, getting sent back to level one and then be like, yeah, that's it.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.000
That's as far as I can get.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:33.320
It definitely cuts back on the amount of tension that you would feel at just any time that you were in a new area or any time that you had inched maybe half a screen forward than you had ever.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:40.540
been before. I feel like if I was any further than I got and didn't have that.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:46.840
I know we've been talking about this for a long time now, but it didn't have that like respawn at the beginning of the level or the checkpoint.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:49.300
And I died in a stupid way.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.280
Like I miss I miss space to jump or something.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.820
I would break my control.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.140
Right. But so if you want to if you're in it to try and beat the game.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.420
Yeah, it's good for this.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:09.500
Yeah. And I'm glad you brought up the you know, like if I missed a jump or something like that, because it's so funny how like that is the smallest thing in this game to have to happen, like to go wrong for you.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:11.400
But even the platforming, right.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:14.660
Even the platforming in this game is incredibly hard.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:20.520
Like they couldn't even give us that much of like, you know, like the platforming is only an extra obstacle for you.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:24.160
It doesn't help you, you know, encounter the enemies differently.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.120
Sometimes the platforming even like makes it this way.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.020
You must pick up an object that you don't want to pick up.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:35.820
Yeah. You know, like because of knockback, you can you can just fall into these pits even even unintentionally.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.020
It's crazy. And I have bad news for you.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.220
You're going to experience a lot of that in Capcom games.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.260
Oh, yeah. Capcom loves knockback for some reason.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.880
And that's just that's just the way they are.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.980
So so we have that real fast.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:57.620
You know, the interesting thing for me on my first impressions, the only thing that's different from you guys that you haven't mentioned yet is I was just shocked that actually like you only get two hits and you're done.

00:11:57.720 --> 00:12:02.600
You know, it's like there's this isn't like Super Mario Brothers where you can find another mushroom or something like that.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.040
Yeah, there is a chance to find armor.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.320
It's incredibly rare and almost like not like twice considerate non-existent.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:23.540
And I would I would say that their pickups are very misleading because in even the beginning stage, not even the first stage, but like in the first screen of the game, you can kill a zombie, which looks like a clown.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:29.640
You can kill a zombie and it'll drop what looks like a one up or just an arm of armor.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:30.720
Right. And it's nothing.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.400
It's just 500 points or something like that.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.620
And it's funny because I mean, like just 500 points is bad, but I mean, and hopefully it's more.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.080
But like this is another game.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.780
We were talking about this in the Super Mario Brothers episode where like collecting coins is pretty imperative.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:53.220
But it's another game where like, you know, there's there's points at lives, you know, like extra lives at 20,000, 70,000 and then every 70,000 after that.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:57.720
But it's like when you have a continue system like this, I don't give a crap about the lives.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.140
Yeah. And that is the other thing.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:03.540
The points that you mentioned, I noticed I never really look at points or care about points.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:07.080
But I did notice that when you continue, you start back at zero points.

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:10.000
Yeah. So if you are going for a high score, then you don't want.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:17.380
Yeah. I mean, I think that's mandatory in any game that like if you if you lose, it should be game over on your high score because at least something should go.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.100
Some kind of permanence should be gone.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.400
All right. So we've talked about that.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:29.720
One thing before we get too much deeper into the game, I'd like to bring up that this game comes out nine days after Super Mario Brothers in the arcade.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:35.020
So like Super Mario Brothers comes out for NES nine days later, you have Ghost and Goblins.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:39.560
And I just think like, you know, these are two pretty big titles around the same time period.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:47.720
And even though it took a little bit longer to get to the NES, it's like these are these are longer form, you know, platforming style games.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:54.000
And I think, you know, I wonder what would have happened if Ghost and Goblins would have beat Mario to the punch.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.380
I'm not sure.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:14:00.700
And also the the arcade version of this game looks leaps and bounds better than the NES version.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:04.840
Oh, yeah. Of either Ghost and Goblins or Super Mario Brothers.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:10.400
So I think if I don't know how much timing would have come since they were this close to each other.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.760
I don't think that Ghost and Goblins would be the new standard.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:19.740
Yeah. It makes me wonder if like, you know, even just like a couple of months, because I mean, back then development didn't take years.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:25.140
So it makes me wonder of like, if this game would have came out like three to four months before Super Mario Brothers and been a success.

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:30.240
Would Miyamoto, you know, look back on the game and been like, maybe we should make it harder.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:35.380
Maybe we should. Arthur would be the would be like the title character of the Nintendo instead of Mario.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:38.140
Yeah. It's interesting to think about.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:50.820
And, you know, I don't have an answer there, but it's just kind of cool to see like these games come out so close to each other and be kind of like at the time, the big games of their respective, like, you know, entries.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:55.700
Yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.480
Cool. So we know about Arthur.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.360
